From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexey Makhalov <alexey.makhalov@broadcom.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mount: associate unconfined_r with mount_roles

Rootless containerd execs /usr/bin/mount from a user session labeled
unconfined_u:unconfined_r:container_runtime_t with MCS.  mount_t is
valid only for roles in mount_roles; only system_r was a member, so
security_compute_sid failed for unconfined_r:mount_t:MCS (SELINUX_ERR,
EACCES on exec).

unconfined_domain(mount_t) is already present in mount.te; add the
missing role association so user logins can run mount in mount_t.

Made-with: Cursor
---
 policy/modules/system/mount.te | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

--- a/policy/modules/system/mount.te
+++ b/policy/modules/system/mount.te
@@ -7,6 +7,14 @@
 
 attribute_role mount_roles;
 roleattribute system_r mount_roles;
+optional_policy(`
+	gen_require(`
+		role unconfined_r;
+	')
+	# Allow user sessions (e.g. SSH logins) to run mount(8) in mount_t
+	# when transitioning from container_runtime_t and similar domains.
+	roleattribute unconfined_r mount_roles;
+')
 
 type mount_t;
 type mount_exec_t;
